---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import cookbooks from '../../data/jev/cookbooks.json';
---
<Base title="Jev evaluation notebook · Amaljith Kuttamath" description="Notes and reproducible probes on Jev: classification outputs, prompt revisions, agent traces, and observed limitations.">
<div class="jev">
  <header class="j-notebook-header">
    <div class="j-notebook-top"><a class="j-back" href="/apps">← Experiments</a><span class="j-kicker">RESEARCH NOTES / 01</span></div>
    <h1>Evaluating Jev</h1>
    <p class="j-lead">I’m testing how typed judgments behave across classification, prompt changes, and tool selection. These are small, inspectable probes. They don’t establish benchmark accuracy.</p>
    <div class="j-notebook-meta"><span>Amaljith Kuttamath</span><span>17–18 Sep 2026</span><code>jev-latest</code><a href="#j-method">Method &amp; limitations ↓</a></div>
  </header>
  <div class="j-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Evaluation view"><button data-mode="labs" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span> Task probes</button><button data-mode="agent" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span> Agent traces</button><button data-mode="prompts" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span> Prompt revisions</button><span class="j-mode-note">EXPLORATORY · NOT A BENCHMARK</span></div>

  <section id="j-labs" aria-label="Task probes">
    <div id="jl-tasks" class="jl-tasks" role="group" aria-label="Choose a classification task"></div>
    <div class="jl-heading"><div><h2 id="jl-title"></h2><p id="jl-description"></p></div><a id="jl-source" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Recipe reference ↗</a></div>
    <div class="jl-examples"><label for="jl-example">SAVED INPUT</label><select id="jl-example"></select><button id="jl-restore" class="j-secondary">Restore example</button></div>
    <div class="j-prompt-grid jl-grid">
      <div class="j-prompt-input"><div id="jl-fields"></div><div class="j-export"><button id="jl-run" class="j-primary" disabled>Classify live</button><button id="jl-stop" class="j-secondary" hidden>Stop</button><button id="jl-copy" class="j-secondary">Copy request</button><a href="https://console.typesafe.ai/decode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Playground ↗</a></div><p id="jl-runtime" class="j-runtime"></p><p id="jl-status" class="j-runtime" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><details class="j-data-detail"><summary>Inspect state, questions &amp; criteria</summary><pre id="jl-request"></pre></details></div>
      <div class="j-prompt-output"><div class="j-section-head"><h3 class="jl-results-title">Model output</h3><span id="jl-origin" class="j-badge"></span></div><div id="jl-results"></div><div class="jl-threshold"><label for="jl-threshold">Review threshold <output id="jl-threshold-value" for="jl-threshold">80%</output></label><input id="jl-threshold" type="range" min="50" max="99" value="80" step="1" /><p>Illustrative policy applied in code. This cutoff is not calibrated; moving it does not rerun inference.</p></div><p id="jl-meta" class="j-meta"></p><button id="jl-download" class="j-secondary" disabled>Download result JSON</button><details class="j-data-detail"><summary>Exact response</summary><pre id="jl-response"></pre></details></div>
    </div>
    <p id="jl-note" class="j-prompt-note"></p>
  </section>

  <section id="j-agent" aria-label="Agent traces" hidden>
    <div class="j-scenario-row"><span class="j-kicker">SAVED SCENARIO</span><div class="j-scenarios" role="group" aria-label="Agent scenarios"><button data-scenario="replacement" aria-pressed="true">Damaged item</button><button data-scenario="out-of-stock" aria-pressed="false">Out of stock</button><button data-scenario="expired" aria-pressed="false">Outside the policy</button></div></div>
    <div class="j-composer"><label for="j-prompt">INPUT / SYNTHETIC CUSTOMER REQUEST</label><textarea id="j-prompt" rows="2" maxlength="1500" spellcheck="false"></textarea><div class="j-composer-bottom"><p><span class="j-workspace-dot"></span> Demo workspace · no real orders are changed</p><div><button id="j-load" class="j-secondary">Load recorded run</button><button id="j-run" class="j-primary" disabled>Run live agent</button><button id="j-stop" class="j-secondary" hidden>Stop</button></div></div><p id="j-runtime" class="j-runtime" role="status"></p></div>
    <div class="j-desk">
      <section class="j-trace-pane" aria-labelledby="j-trace-heading"><div class="j-section-head"><h2 id="j-trace-heading">Execution trace</h2><span id="j-source" class="j-badge">RECORDED RUN</span></div><p id="j-trace-meta" class="j-meta"></p><div id="j-trace" class="j-trace"></div><p id="j-run-status" class="j-run-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></section>
      <aside class="j-inspector" aria-label="Inspect a decision"><div class="j-section-head"><h2>Selected step</h2><span class="j-kicker" id="j-step-number"></span></div><div id="j-decision"></div><details class="j-raw"><summary>Exact request &amp; response <span>＋</span></summary><pre id="j-raw-decision"></pre></details><div id="j-workspace" class="j-workspace"></div></aside>
    </div>
    <div class="j-footnote"><strong>Method</strong><p>Jev selects a tool and closed-set arguments in one request. Deep Agents executes the selected Python function, then passes its result back. Code enforces the demo’s policy. Expand a step to inspect its probabilities and returned data.</p></div>
  </section>

  <section id="j-prompts" aria-label="Prompt revisions" hidden>
    <div class="j-prompt-select"><label for="j-example">SAVED QUESTION SET</label><select id="j-example"><option value="sarcasm">Sentiment · sarcastic praise</option><option value="quoted_opinion">Sentiment · quoted criticism</option><option value="code_guard">Code · reversed guard</option><option value="code_valid">Code · correct guard</option><option value="code_guard-refined" selected>Code · refined repair question</option><option value="code_valid-refined">Code · refined correct guard</option><option value="browser_next">Action · subscription active</option><option value="browser_done">Action · cancellation complete</option></select></div>
    <div class="j-prompt-grid"><div class="j-prompt-input"><label for="j-state">State</label><textarea id="j-state" rows="9" spellcheck="false"></textarea><details class="j-question-edit"><summary>Edit the questions <span>＋</span></summary><label class="j-sr" for="j-questions">Questions JSON</label><textarea id="j-questions" rows="16" spellcheck="false"></textarea></details><div class="j-export"><button id="j-copy" class="j-primary">Copy request</button><button id="j-restore" class="j-secondary">Restore</button><a href="https://console.typesafe.ai/decode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Playground ↗</a></div><p id="j-edit-status" role="status" class="j-runtime"></p></div><div class="j-prompt-output"><span class="j-badge">RECORDED ANSWERS</span><div id="j-answers"></div><p id="j-prompt-note" class="j-prompt-note"></p></div></div>
  </section>

  <section id="j-method" class="j-method" aria-labelledby="j-method-title">
    <div class="j-section-head"><h2 id="j-method-title">Method &amp; limitations</h2><span class="j-kicker">READ BEFORE GENERALIZING</span></div>
    <div class="j-method-grid">
      <div><h3>Sample &amp; procedure</h3><p>15 hand-authored classification examples across six tasks, eight prompt trials, and three agent traces. Saved requests and responses were recorded on September 17–18, 2026. Inputs are synthetic. There is no held-out test set or aggregate accuracy estimate.</p><p>Edit a task input to run a new classification. Each response belongs to the exact state and question set shown. The model alias <code>jev-latest</code> may change over time.</p></div>
      <div><h3>What the outputs mean</h3><p><code>Choice</code> returns a distribution over labels. <code>Noul</code> estimates a yes probability. <code>Score</code> applies an ordered rubric. Selected-label probability is distinct from the API’s confidence field; neither establishes correctness.</p><p>Latency is a single observed request duration, not a controlled speed benchmark. Review thresholds and composite weights are illustrative policies.</p></div>
      <div class="j-observation"><h3>Observed failure</h3><p>In the reversed-guard code probe, the comparison on <code>L2</code> needs repair. Jev selects <code>L3</code>, including after prompt refinement. Both requests and their original responses remain in <strong>Prompt revisions</strong>.</p><p>Agent traces use a bounded synthetic workspace. Code enforces policy; Jev selects tools and closed-set arguments. Live agent execution requires the local Deep Agents runtime.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <details class="jl-cookbooks"><summary><span><strong>Cookbook reference notes</strong><span class="j-kicker">18 RECIPES / REVIEWED 18 SEP 2026</span></span><span aria-hidden="true">＋</span></summary><p>Provider recipes mapped to applications and evaluation caveats. These are documentation notes; the workflows have not all been reproduced here.</p><div class="j-table-scroll" role="region" aria-label="Cookbook references" tabindex="0"><table class="j-reference-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Recipe</th><th scope="col">Pattern &amp; application</th><th scope="col">Evaluation caveat</th></tr></thead><tbody>{cookbooks.map(recipe => <tr><th scope="row"><a href={recipe.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{recipe.title} ↗</a><span class="j-kicker">{recipe.family}</span></th><td><p>{recipe.pattern}</p><p>{recipe.application}</p></td><td>{recipe.limit}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details>
  <footer class="j-provenance"><p>Evaluation notebook by Amaljith Kuttamath. Recorded outputs are preserved as returned, including misses. Inspect or download the raw responses alongside each probe.</p><a href="https://github.com/amaljithkuttamath/amaljithkuttamath.github.io/tree/main/src/data/jev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Recorded data ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/amaljithkuttamath/amaljithkuttamath.github.io/tree/main/agent" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Runtime &amp; setup ↗</a></footer>
  <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to inspect the interactive traces. The source repository includes every recorded request and result.</p></noscript>
</div>
</Base>
<script>import '../../lib/jev/ui'; import '../../lib/jev/labs-ui';</script>
<style is:global>@import '../../styles/jev.css';</style>
